<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wismar Tribunal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1653</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wismar">Wismar</a> Tribunal was the supreme court of appeal for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s German possessions, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Swedish Pomerania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen-verden">Bremen-Verden</a> and Wismar, set up at Wismar in 1653. It replaced appeals to the courts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, which Sweden's territories were exempted from under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>. It moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a> after Sweden pawned Wismar in 1803.</p></div>
